{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972446-wendigo-bloodlines","id":972446,"title":"Wendigo bloodlines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T04:08:37-07:00","id":972446,"title":"Wendigo bloodlines","content":"From the new slices of the 20thMET pdf :<br /> <br /> ''<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MinionCYR-Regular\">The revival of Russian and Siberian bloodlines thought long-extinct has proven to be a boon to the numbers of the tribe. Lineages thought dormant from the Russian steppes hear the song of Wendigo and now rise at the beckoning of their totem. The influx of new and old blood caused some division within the tribe\u2019s conservative elements, but most agree that their bond with Wendigo matters far more than ties of blood. The Silver Fangs have begun to take interest in rumors that the Siberkah rise once more. The Shadow Lords also have a vested interest in discovering the reason why these lines have returned, as the last thing they want is a closer tie between the Wendigo and the Silver Fangs.''<br /> <br /> Do you use it also in your pen e paper chronicles?<br /> What's your suggestions?<br /> On a realistic point of view , wendigo blood spreaded also among people of siberian origins ( sami,huns,magyars, ecc.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:08:24-07:00","id":972472,"title":"","content":"My last Silver Fang PC was from a Crescent Moon bloodline that had ties to the Siberakh. Each Generation, one Cub was destined to lend aid to the Siberakh on an important mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:21:04-07:00","id":972506,"title":"","content":"Thought long extinct? There were literally hundreds of them in Rage Across Russia, which was published in 1993.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T21:41:29-07:00","id":972935,"title":"","content":"I don't use them. The Siberakh is an example of a plot point that should only exist if your chronicle intends to focus on them. If they don't, there is no reason for them to exist. Personally I am not interested in the chronicle concept of a lost, new or pseudo-tribe, and if I was I still wouldn't be using the Siberakh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:16:14-07:00","id":972978,"title":"","content":"The problem is that, if the wendigo siberian blood is awakening, well, a lot of steppe tribes can have wendigo blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T02:31:39-07:00","id":973005,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't import the BNS setting changes to a TT WtA game unless that was the premise I started the game under. I think the changes have a lot of potential to them, but if I'm running W20, I generally intend to run W20; not W20 + BNS Werewolf.<br /> <br /> In my every evolving homebrewed &quot;reboot&quot; of the setting, this was something I wanted to work in because of a number of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:18:51-07:00","id":973124,"title":"","content"