"message\">Yeah, that was my point. The things we don't like about BNS Werewolf <i>Metaplot</i> come straight from Paradox. The things we don't like about BNS Werewolf <i>Mechanics</i> are BNS original.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because this stuff predated the Paradox buyout? Onyx path stuff is just as likely to &quot;build to the new metaplot&quot; as any BNS stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:19:06-07:00","id":974185,"title":"","content":"BNS did say that their Werewolf had more communication with WW during development. But it's way to early to say how much WW will keep when WtA 5e finally rolls out even if WW had a lot of say in BNS Werewolf's development or just some ideas and contributions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T10:31:16-07:00","id":974504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972446-wendigo-bloodlines?p=972506#post972506\" rel=\"nofol